From 8e17cefd0e24b84e069dc810a0acd253495b6959 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VLCKit Aloha Release <devnull@alohabrowser.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 09:27:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] modules: codec: avcodec: pin max_pixels/max_samples to
 INT64_MAX
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Follow-up to 0021 (NULL codec_whitelist before avcodec_open2). On iPhone
15 with -aloha10, opening a Downloads folder no longer crashes, but
non-mp4 video thumbnails never render — the placeholder icon stays in
place. Diagnostic logging from TSVLCThumbnailGenerator on the app side
confirms libvlc_media_thumbnail_request_by_pos queues fine and the
MediaThumbnailGenerated event fires within ~1s, but with
p_thumbnail = NULL.

Earlier device-side runtime log already had the smoking gun:

  [mpeg4 @ ...] [IMGUTILS @ ...] Picture size 1280x720 exceeds
  specified max pixel count 0, see the documentation if you wish to
  increase it
  [hevc_videotoolbox @ ...] [IMGUTILS @ ...] Picture size 1920x960
  exceeds specified max pixel count 0, ...

FFmpeg's av_image_check_size2() rejects any decoded frame when
AVCodecContext.max_pixels is < INT64_MAX AND smaller than the actual
picture. The default value for max_pixels (per
libavcodec/options_table.h) is INT_MAX, set by av_opt_set_defaults()
inside avcodec_alloc_context3(). On simulator the default sticks and
thumbnails generate. On the iPhone 15 static-link path packaged via
aloha_ld_r_repack.py, the field is observed = 0 by the time the
decoder runs, so EVERY frame fails the check and the decoder bails
out without producing a picture — exactly matching the NULL
p_thumbnail callback we see in the diagnostic logs.

This is the same flavour of defaults-getting-clobbered issue as 0021
(codec_whitelist). Same surgical fix: explicitly assign the documented
defaults right before avcodec_open2 so the decoder runs as intended
regardless of why av_opt_set_defaults's writes didn't stick:

  ctx->max_pixels   = INT64_MAX;  // 'no pixel limit'
  ctx->max_samples  = INT64_MAX;  // same for audio

INT64_MAX (>= the AVOption upper bound INT_MAX) is the canonical 'no
limit' sentinel; FFmpeg's check is `max_pixels < INT64_MAX` so this
value disables the check entirely.

Covers both video (OpenVideoCodec) and audio (OpenAudioCodec) paths,
which both funnel through ffmpeg_OpenCodec.
---
 modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c | 48 ++++++++++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c b/modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c
index b89e59e0f2..a48c2036d8 100644
--- a/modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c
+++ b/modules/codec/avcodec/avcodec.c
@@ -289,19 +289,43 @@ int ffmpeg_OpenCodec( decoder_t *p_dec, AVCodecContext *ctx,
         free(psz_opts);
     }
 
-    /* Aloha: explicitly NULL the codec/format whitelist pointers before
-     * avcodec_open2. These fields are nominally zero-initialised by
-     * avcodec_alloc_context3() (which uses av_mallocz), but in static-
-     * library builds of FFmpeg+VLC packaged through aloha_ld_r_repack.py
-     * we have observed them holding stack-garbage values like
-     * 0xFFFFFFFF00000000 by the time OpenVideoCodec runs. FFmpeg's
-     * avcodec_open2 then passes the garbage pointer to av_match_list,
-     * which dereferences it as a char* and crashes the input thread
-     * with KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS. Setting them NULL here is harmless
-     * (NULL = "no whitelist, all codecs allowed", which is what VLC
-     * always intended) and prevents the crash regardless of the
-     * underlying root cause. */
+    /* Aloha: explicitly set AVCodecContext fields that depend on
+     * av_opt_set_defaults() before avcodec_open2. In static-library
+     * builds of FFmpeg+VLC packaged through aloha_ld_r_repack.py we
+     * have observed these fields holding stack-garbage values when
+     * OpenVideoCodec / OpenAudioCodec runs on iPhone 15 (real
+     * device) — but NOT on iOS Simulator. The two reproducible
+     * symptoms:
+     *
+     *   1) ctx->codec_whitelist holding a garbage `char*`. FFmpeg
+     *      then calls av_match_list(codec->name, codec_whitelist, ',')
+     *      from avcodec_open2 -> the input thread crashes with
+     *      KERN_INVALID_ADDRESS (saw 0xFFFFFFFF00000000 and
+     *      0x2e726579616c5065 = ASCII "...ePlayer." on device).
+     *
+     *   2) ctx->max_pixels = 0. FFmpeg's av_image_check_size2 then
+     *      rejects every decoded frame with
+     *        "Picture size 1280x720 exceeds specified max pixel
+     *         count 0, see the documentation if you wish to
+     *         increase it"
+     *      The decoder bails out, libvlc_media_thumbnail_request_by_pos
+     *      emits libvlc_MediaThumbnailGenerated with p_thumbnail=NULL,
+     *      and the Downloads UI keeps showing placeholder icons.
+     *
+     * av_opt_set_defaults() (called inside avcodec_alloc_context3)
+     * is supposed to set max_pixels=INT_MAX, max_samples=INT_MAX,
+     * codec_whitelist=NULL. Something in the device static-link
+     * pipeline is leaving the post-defaults state corrupted. Hard-
+     * setting the values here is harmless (matches the documented
+     * "no limit / no whitelist" defaults) and avoids the crash/
+     * silent-failure cliff regardless of the underlying root cause.
+     *
+     * Same patch covers both the video (OpenVideoCodec) and audio
+     * (OpenAudioCodec) paths because both funnel through this
+     * function. */
     ctx->codec_whitelist = NULL;
+    ctx->max_pixels = INT64_MAX;
+    ctx->max_samples = INT64_MAX;
 
     vlc_avcodec_lock();
     ret = avcodec_open2( ctx, codec, options ? &options : NULL );
-- 
